<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/bailiwick-of-jersey"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bailiwick%20of%20Jersey.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bailiwick of Jersey</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">German forces occupy the island</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-luxembourg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Grand%20Duchy%20of%20Luxembourg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Grand Duchy of Luxembourg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany invades; Grand Duchess Charlotte and the government go into exile</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Greece.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Greece</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Greece rejects Italy’s ultimatum and drives the invaders into Albania</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20the%20Netherlands.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of the Netherlands</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany invades; Rotterdam is bombed and the army capitulates within five days</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union occupies and annexes Lithuania</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Estonia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Estonia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union occupies and annexes Estonia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Latvia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Latvia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union occupies and annexes Latvia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dunkirk evacuation and the Battle of Britain; Churchill becomes Prime Minister</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-indochina"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Indochina.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Indochina</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japanese troops enter northern Indochina after France’s defeat</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-west-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20West%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French West Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Vichy forces repel a British and Free French attack on Dakar</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/indian-independence-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indian%20independence%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indian independence movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Muslim League’s Lahore Resolution demands independent states for the Muslim-majority areas</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-cuba-1902-1959"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Cuba%20(1902-1959).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Cuba (1902-1959)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A new constitution with the rights to labour and health care is adopted, and Batista is elected president.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-third-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Third%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Third Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the Fall of France, parliament gives full powers to Marshal Philippe Pétain</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-romania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Romania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Romania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After territorial losses Carol II abdicates and Ion Antonescu rules with full powers</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania-1918-1940"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania%20(1918-1940).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania (1918-1940)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the Soviet ultimatum of 14 June, Lithuania is annexed as the Lithuanian Soviet Socialist Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tibet-1912-1951"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tibet%20(1912-1951).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tibet (1912-1951)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 14th Dalai Lama was enthroned in Lhasa on the Tibetan New Year</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Pétain signs the armistice with Germany</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The National Assembly grants full powers to Pétain at Vichy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Law on the status of Jews excludes Jews from the administration, the armed forces and many professions</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Pétain and Hitler meet at Montoire, sealing state collaboration</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/francoist-spain"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Francoist%20Spain.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Francoist Spain</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Franco and Hitler meet at Hendaye on 23 October, but the talks on Spain's entry into the Second World War end in failure</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Hungary%20(1920-1946).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Second Vienna Award assigns Northern Transylvania to Hungary</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/northern-rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Northern%20Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Northern Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">African miners strike after European miners win higher pay, and troops of the Northern Rhodesian Regiment fire on them, killing 17</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/winston-churchill"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Winston%20Churchill.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Winston Churchill</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He becomes prime minister and resolves to fight on after the fall of France</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/london"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/London.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>London</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Blitz begins on 7 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/amsterdam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Amsterdam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Amsterdam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nazi Germany invades the Netherlands and occupies Amsterdam until 1945</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/lahore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lahore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lahore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The All India Muslim League passes the Lahore Resolution demanding a separate homeland for the Muslims of India</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/lima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">An earthquake strikes, and rapid growth from migration from the Andes begins</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/lascaux"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lascaux.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lascaux</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Marcel Ravidat and three friends enter the cave, and the Abbé Henri Breuil visits it nine days later</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/nazca-lines"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazca%20Lines.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazca Lines</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Paul Kosok, in Peru to study irrigation systems, flew over the lines and recognised a bird among them</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/stalinism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Stalinism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Stalinism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Trotsky is assassinated in Mexico, the last of Stalin’s opponents among the former party leadership</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/trotskyism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Trotskyism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Trotskyism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ramón Mercader attacks Trotsky in Mexico City on 20 August; Trotsky dies the next day</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/three-principles-of-the-people"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Three%20Principles%20of%20the%20People.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Three Principles of the People</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mao Zedong's On New Democracy reads the Principles as the “New Three Principles of the People”</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Zaki al-Arsuzi founds the Arab Ba'ath on 29 November, and Michel Aflaq and Salah al-Din al-Bitar found the Arab Ihya Movement, later the Arab Ba'ath Movement</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/caodaism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Caodaism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Caodaism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The religion has gathered over a million members, between a fifth and a quarter of the population of Cochinchina</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/spiritism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Spiritism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Spiritism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Brazil’s penal code of 1940 ends the official prohibition of Spiritism</span></li></ul></section>
